  <artifactId>org.eclipse.daanse.olap.xmla.connector.relational.oledb</artifactId>
  <name>Daanse OLAP XMLA Connector — relational rowsets that answer empty</name>
  <description>The DBSCHEMA_* rowsets this server advertises but cannot yet fill. They carry their columns, restrictions and mask, and answer a well-formed empty rowset — an unknown request type is a fault, an empty answer is not. What sorts a rowset into this bundle is that nothing implements it, not where it comes from; that all 28 happen to be OLE DB rather than [MS-SSAS] follows from the fact that a real Analysis Services advertises only four DBSCHEMA rowsets, and those four are implemented. The bundle holds no implementation and depends on nothing but the API, so leaving it out costs no function at all — only 28 advertisements. When one of them is filled, it moves to the sibling bundle. What filling them needs is a richer catalog model; see the handover note in the xmla repository.</description>

